\ lib/doc/report.1z - Cross-reference report for undocumented public words
\
\ Cross-references runtime introspection (word-info) against the source-level
\ doc-comment map produced by lib/doc/extract.1z to flag public words that lack
\ a doc-comment, and formats the per-word warning emitted during documentation
\ generation. This is the generation-time counterpart to the linter's
\ `missing-doc-comment` rule; the linter remains the authoritative lint check.

use "strings" ;
use "sequences" ;

\\ Whether a word should appear in the documentation's undocumented check. A
\\ word is public when it is not a native primitive, was not auto-generated
\\ (carries no provenance), and is not a private word whose name starts with
\\ `(`. Mirrors the linter's `(skip-word?)`, negated.
public-word?: ( wi -- ? ) [
  dup native?>> [
    drop f
  ] [
    dup provenance>> f = not [
      drop f
    ] [
      name>> >string "(" #starts-with? not
    ] if
  ] if
] ;

\\ Whether a public word lacks a doc-comment, given the module's source-level
\\ doc-comment map. True when the word is public and has neither a source-level
\\ doc-comment (its name is absent from the doc-map) nor an introspection
\\ `doc>>` string. This is the same condition under which the generator renders
\\ a word as undocumented, restricted to public words.
undocumented-public-word?: ( doc-map wi -- ? ) [
  dup public-word? [
    dup doc>> f = [
      name>> @has? not
    ] [
      2drop f
    ] if
  ] [
    2drop f
  ] if
] ;

\\ Format the stderr warning for an undocumented public word, citing its source
\\ location: `{rel}:{line}: warning: undocumented public word '{name}'`. When
\\ the line is unknown (`f`), the `:line` segment is omitted.
format-undocumented-warning: ( rel line name -- str ) [
  [
    dup f =
    [ drop ]
    [ >string ":" swap #append #append ]
    if
    ": warning: undocumented public word '" #append
  ] dip
  #append "'" #append
] ;
